nised"],"about":"C. Kandaswami Naidu College for Women is one of the oldest educational institutions in Cuddalore. The college was established in 1967 through an endowment created by Pachaiyappa''s Trust in memory of Thiru. Condavru Kandaswami Naidu. It began functioning at Cuddalore on 15 July 1967 and initially started with Pre-University classes and undergraduate programmes in Economics and Tamil. The institution was subsequently shifted to its present Semmandalam campus on 4 October 1968. The college states that it was the first women''s college in Cuddalore district.\\n\\nThe institution is a unit of Pachaiyappa''s Trust and is currently affiliated to Thiruvalluvar University, Vellore. The college provides teaching, recreational and sporting facilities for women students and conducts both academic and student-development activities. Its current official website lists Day College, Research Courses and Evening Classes, while its 2025-26 prospectus provides programme, eligibility, admission and fee information. The institution also operates student-support and extension activities including NSS, NCC, Youth Red Cross, SC/ST Cell, career guidance and placement, counselling, anti-ragging, women grievance and environmental activities.","highlights":["Established on 15 July 1967","First women''s college in Cuddalore district","Unit of Pachaiyappa''s Trust","Currently affiliated to Thiruvalluvar University, Vellore","Located at Semmandalam, Cuddalore","Offers undergraduate and postgraduate programmes","Provides Day College and Shift II / Evening College options","Student activities include NSS, NCC and Youth Red Cross","Career Guidance and Placement Cell is constituted","Government-supported scholarship and student welfare schemes are implemented"],"departments":[{"name":"B.A. Tamil","level":"UG"},{"name":"B.A. English","level":"UG"},{"name":"B.A. History","level":"UG"},{"name":"B.A. Economics","level":"UG"},{"name":"B.Sc. Mathematics","level":"UG"},{"name":"B.Sc. Chemi