nt-Arts-College-Namakkal-collegeshine_4_11zon.webp","type":"website","url":null},"twitterCard":{"card":"summary_large_image","title":"Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Namakkal - CollegeShine","description":"Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Namakkal is a government arts & science college in Namakkal established in 1968. Named for Arignar Anna, serving.","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Arignar-Anna-Government-Arts-College-Namakkal-collegeshine_4_11zon.webp"},"structuredData":{"schemaType":"CollegeOrUniversity","jsonLd":null,"includeFaqSchema":true,"includeBreadcrumbSchema":true}},"name":"Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Namakkal","shortName":"AAGAC Namakkal","tagline":"Named for Arignar Anna, serving Namakkal since 1968","category":"arts-science","type":"Degree College","ownership":"Government","established":"1968","location":"Namakkal","district":"Namakkal","address":"Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Mohanur-Namakkal Road, Sanyasikaradu Post, Namakkal - 637002, Tamil Nadu, India","mapLink":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Arignar+Anna+Government+Arts+College+Namakkal","mapQuery":"Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Namakkal, Tamil Nadu 637002","website":"https://aagacnkl.edu.in/","phone":"04286-266323","email":"principal@aagacnkl.edu.in","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Arignar-Anna-Government-Arts-College-Namakkal-collegeshine_4_11zon.webp","videoUrl":null,"affiliation":"Periyar University, Salem","accreditation":["NAAC B (Re-accredited)"],"about":"Arignar Anna Government Arts College, Namakkal was established in the 1968-69 academic year and named after C.N. Annadurai (Arignar Anna), the former Chief Minister of Tamil Nadu. The founding effort was driven by local leaders including Pavalar P. Muthusamy, a former MLA of Namakkal, and V. Chockalingam, a former Namakkal Revenue Divisional Officer. Originally affiliated to the University of Madras and temporarily housed in a government high school, the college moved to its permanent campus on Namakkal-Mohanur Road in 1970-71 and today functions under Periyar University, Salem, holding a re-accredited B grade from NAAC.\\n\\nThe institution now offers 14 undergraduate programmes, 11 postgraduate programmes, and 8 each of M.Phil and Ph.D programmes across departments such as English, Economics, Physics, Chemistry and Botany. Its emblem, featuring a notebook, pen and traditional lamp alongside Namakkal''s rock fort and temples, reflects the college''s rootedness in local heritage alongside its educational mission. The college continues to serve first-generation learners from Namakkal town and its surrounding rural taluks.","highlights":["Established 1968-69, named after former CM Arignar Anna","Affiliated to Periyar University, Salem","NAAC B grade (re-accredited)","Offers 14 UG, 11 PG, 8 M.Phil and 8 Ph.D programmes","Moved to permanent Mohanur Road campus in 1970-71"],"departments":[{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"}],"facilities":["Available"],"placementRate":36,"avgPackage":"≈₹60,000","highestPackage":"≈₹65,000","placementYear":null,"admissionProcess":["Merit-based admission per Tamil Nadu Government / TNGASA norms","10+2 pass required for UG entry","Relevant Bachelor''s degree required for PG entry"],"scholarships":["Government Scholarship Support","Post Matric Scholarship Support","First Graduate Scholarship Support","BC / MBC Scholarship Support","SC / ST Scholarship Support","Minority Scholarship Support"],"events":["Academic Events","Cultural Events","Sports Activities","NSS Activities","NCC Activities","Student Development Programmes"],"distanceInfo":{"status":"Distance information is currently being updated"},"hostelFeatures":["Hostel Facility","Stu