/07/Government-Arts-College-for-Men-Krishnagiri_7_11zon.webp","type":"website","url":null},"twitterCard":{"card":"summary_large_image","title":"Government Arts College for Women, Krishnagiri - CollegeShine","description":"Government Arts College for Women, Krishnagiri is a government arts & science college in Rayakotta Road, Krishnagiri established in 1992. Empowering women of.","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Government-Arts-College-for-Men-Krishnagiri_7_11zon.webp"},"structuredData":{"schemaType":"CollegeOrUniversity","jsonLd":null,"includeFaqSchema":true,"includeBreadcrumbSchema":true}},"name":"Government Arts College for Women, Krishnagiri","shortName":"GACW Krishnagiri","tagline":"Empowering women of Krishnagiri district since 1992","category":"arts-science","type":"Degree College (Women)","ownership":"Government","established":"1992","location":"Rayakotta Road, Krishnagiri","district":"Krishnagiri","address":"Government Arts College for Women, Rayakotta Road, Krishnagiri - 635001/635002, Tamil Nadu, India","mapLink":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Government+Arts+College+for+Women+Krishnagiri","mapQuery":"Government Arts College for Women, Krishnagiri, Tamil Nadu 635002","website":"https://www.gacwkgi.org/","phone":"04343-225934","email":"gacwkgi@rediffmail.com","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Government-Arts-College-for-Men-Krishnagiri_7_11zon.webp","videoUrl":null,"affiliation":"Periyar University, Salem","accreditation":[],"about":"Government Arts College for Women, Krishnagiri was established in 1992 to meet the higher-education needs of women in Krishnagiri district, many from underprivileged rural backgrounds. It began academic operations that year with 112 students, initially named Annai Sandhiya Government Arts College for Women per G.O. No. 800 dated 26/08/1993, before being renamed to its present title under Government Order No. 569 dated 12/01/1997. The college is affiliated to Periyar University, Salem and is located on Rayakotta Road on a campus of around 5.28 hectares.\\n\\nThe college now enrolls close to 3,000 students across 12 undergraduate, 7 postgraduate and 2 research programmes in departments including Tamil, Commerce, Mathematics, Physics, Statistics, Chemistry and Biochemistry, having introduced a shift system in 2007 to accommodate growing demand. It provides well-equipped departmental laboratories, a library, and an active placement cell that runs training and awareness workshops for final-year students, though detailed placement statistics are not widely published. The institution positions itself as a dedicated women-only learning environment offering affordable, government-subsidised higher education to the district''s students.","highlights":["Established 1992 to serve women of Krishnagiri district","Affiliated to Periyar University, Salem","Shift system introduced in 2007 to expand access","Offers 12 UG, 7 PG and 2 research programmes","Campus spans approximately 5.28 hectares (~13 acres)"],"departments":[{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"},{"name":null,"level":"UG"}],"facilities":["Gym","Library","Sports facilities","IT infrastructure","Cafeteria","Auditorium","Departmental laboratories"],"placementRate":0,"avgPackage":null,"highestPackage":null,"placementYear":null,"admissionProcess":["10+2 pass required for UG admission","Bachelor''s degree required for PG admission","Merit-based selection per Government and Periyar University norms"],"scholarships":[],"events":[],"distanceInfo":{},"hostelFeatures":[],"technicalClubs":[],"culturalClubs":[],"communityService":[]}'),
