],"about":"Government Arts and Science College, Sathyamangalam was established in 2016 and is affiliated to Bharathiar University, Coimbatore. The college is situated on a 9.7-acre campus on the outskirts of Sathyamangalam in Erode District. It was established with three undergraduate programmes in Commerce, Economics and English with an initial strength of 180 students. The institution has subsequently expanded its academic offerings and currently functions with 11 undergraduate degree programmes and more than 1,000 students.\\n\\nThe college is recognised under Sections 2(f) and 12(B) of the UGC Act 1956 and has received NAAC accreditation with a B Grade and 2.25 CGPA in its first cycle. The campus includes classrooms, six computer and science laboratories, a library with INFLIBNET facility, a conference hall with approximately 500-seat capacity, cafeteria, Wi-Fi connectivity, RO drinking water and separate parking facilities. The institution also provides NSS, Youth Red Cross, Yoga, sports, Computer Literacy Programme, TNPSC coaching and placement and career guidance activities.","highlights":["Established in 2016","Government of Tamil Nadu Institution","9.7-Acre Campus","Affiliated to Bharathiar University","UGC 2(f) and 12(B) Recognition","NAAC B Grade Accreditation","2.25 NAAC CGPA","1,000+ Students","60 Faculty Members","6 Computer and Science Laboratories","5,575+ Library Books","INFLIBNET Library Facility","500-Seat Conference Hall","Wi-Fi Enabled Campus","NSS and Youth Red Cross Activities"],"departments":[{"name":"Commerce","level":"UG"},{"name":"Economics","level":"UG"},{"name":"English","level":"UG"},{"name":"Mathematics","level":"UG"},{"name":"Computer Science","level":"UG"},{"name":"Computer Applications","level":"UG"},{"name":"Business Administration","level":"UG"},{"name":"Visual Communication","level":"UG"},{"name":"Physics","level":"UG"},{"name":"Chemistry","level":"UG"},{"name":"Botany","level":"UG"}],"facilities":[{"icon":"ti-wifi","name":"Campu