e of Rehabilitation Medicine - CollegeShine","description":"Government Institute of Rehabilitation Medicine, Chennai is a government physiotherapy college in K.K. Nagar, Chennai established in 1979. Pioneering Center.","image":"https://i3c-medical-colleges-assets.blr1.digitaloceanspaces.com/2025/04/11/9921e87146e346dba3659835a31e9d3f.jpg","type":"website","url":null},"twitterCard":{"card":"summary_large_image","title":"Government Institute of Rehabilitation Medicine - CollegeShine","description":"Government Institute of Rehabilitation Medicine, Chennai is a government physiotherapy college in K.K. Nagar, Chennai established in 1979. Pioneering Center.","image":"https://i3c-medical-colleges-assets.blr1.digitaloceanspaces.com/2025/04/11/9921e87146e346dba3659835a31e9d3f.jpg"},"structuredData":{"schemaType":"CollegeOrUniversity","jsonLd":null,"includeFaqSchema":true,"includeBreadcrumbSchema":true}},"name":"Government Institute of Rehabilitation Medicine, Chennai","shortName":"GIRM Chennai","tagline":"Pioneering Center for Medical Rehabilitation & Prosthetics in India","category":"physiotherapy","type":"Government College / Institute","ownership":"Government","established":1979,"location":"K.K. Nagar, Chennai","district":"Chennai","address":"Government College of Physiotherapy, K.K. Nagar, Ashok Nagar, Chennai, Tamil Nadu 600083","mapLink":"https://maps.google.com/?q=Government+Institute+of+Rehabilitation+Medicine+K.K.+Nagar+Chennai","mapQuery":"Government+Institute+of+Rehabilitation+Medicine+KK+Nagar+Chennai","website":"http://www.tn.gov.in/","phone":"044-24892678","email":"mailto:webadmin@tn.gov.in","image":"https://i3c-medical-colleges-assets.blr1.digitaloceanspaces.com/2025/04/11/9921e87146e346dba3659835a31e9d3f.jpg","videoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/z71mID9xcf4?si=y9XGN1AqwetinQ4Q&amp;start=204","affiliation":"Affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University, Chennai; attached to Directorate of Medical Education","accreditation":["Recognized by UGC","Affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University","Government of Tamil Nadu Institution","Attached to Directorate of Medical Education"],"about":"Government Institute of Rehabilitation Medicine (GIRM) is a state-owned institution and hospital situated in K.K. Nagar, Chennai. Founded in 1979, it is funded and managed by the Government of Tamil Nadu and is attached to the Directorate of Medical Education. It is affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University, Chennai and recognized by the UGC.\\n\\nGIRM is a pioneering center in India for medical rehabilitation, particularly noted for its historic contributions to prosthetics — including the development of the ''Madras Foot'' in 1968, a design later adapted into the well-known Jaipur foot. Tamil Nadu was the first state in India to start a three-year diploma course in orthotics and prosthetics in the late 1960s, conducted through the orthopaedics department of Madras Medical College, which laid the groundwork for GIRM''s establishment. The institute is also the only government-run centre in Tamil Nadu that manufactures prosthetic limbs. Today, GIRM offers a Bachelor of Physiotherapy (B.P.T.) programme, with classrooms equipped with audio-visual aids, specialized labs for anatomy, physiology and biomechanics, a library, and computer/internet facilities for academic use.","highlights":["Established in 1979 by Government of Tamil Nadu","Only Government-Run Centre for Prosthetic Limbs in India","Originator of the ''Madras Foot'' Prosthetic Design (1968)","Affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University","Attached to Directorate of Medical Education","Offers Bachelor of Physiotherapy (B.P.T.)","Specialized Labs for Anatomy, Physiology & Biomechanics","Well-Stocked Library with Physiotherapy Resources","Computer Lab & Internet Facilities","Historic Pioneer of Orthotics & Prosthetics Training in India"],"departments":[{"name":"Bachelor of Physiotherapy (BPT)","level":"UG"}],"facilities":[{"