dindigul@gmail.com","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/government-medical-college-dindigul.webp","videoUrl":"","affiliation":"Affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University; functions under the Directorate of Medical Education (DME), Government of Tamil Nadu","accreditation":["Government Institution under DME, Tamil Nadu","Affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University","Recognized by National Medical Commission (NMC)","Empanelled with Tamil Nadu Medical Services Corporation (TNMSC)"],"about":"Government Medical College and Hospital, Dindigul, functions under the Directorate of Medical Education, Chennai, Tamil Nadu, since 1 March 2021. Alongside its MBBS programme (5 batches of 150 students each), the college runs an Allied Health Sciences wing offering the Bachelor of Science in Medical Laboratory Technology (B.Sc. MLT) and a range of certificate-level paramedical courses.\\n\\nThe B.Sc. MLT programme is a 3-year, 6-semester undergraduate course combining theoretical knowledge with hands-on laboratory training in Biochemistry, Microbiology, Hematology, Clinical Pathology, Immunology & Serology, Blood Banking, and Histopathology & Cytology. Graduates are trained in sample collection, use of advanced laboratory equipment, and diagnostic testing, preparing them for roles as medical laboratory technicians, laboratory supervisors, blood bank technologists, and quality control analysts. The college additionally offers certificate courses in Emergency Care Technician, Dialysis Technician, Anaesthesia Technician, Theatre Technician, Orthopedic Technician, and Multipurpose Health Worker (MPHW), reflecting its focus on building a skilled allied healthcare workforce for the region.","highlights":["B.Sc. MLT — 3-Year, 6-Semester Programme","6 Allied Healthcare Certificate Courses (Emergency Care, Dialysis, Anaesthesia, Theatre, Ortho Technician, MPHW)","Functions Under Directorate of Medical Education, Tamil Nadu (Since 2021)","Affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University","Attached Government Hospital with Multiple Clinical Departments","Hands-On Training in Modern Laboratory Equipment","Central Library & Separate Hostel Facilities","Government Institution — Affordable Fee Structure"],"departments":[{"name":"B.Sc. MLT (Medical Laboratory Technology)","level":"UG"},{"name":"Certificate — Emergency Care Technician","level":"UG"},{"name":"Certificate — Dialysis Technician","level":"UG"},{"name":"Certificate — Anaesthesia Technician","level":"UG"},{"name":"Certificate — Theatre Technician","level":"UG"},{"name":"Certificate — Orthopedic Technician","level":"UG"},{"name":"Certificate — Multipurpose Health Worker (MPHW)","level":"UG"}],"facilities":[{"icon":"ti-wifi","name":"Campus Network"},{"icon":"ti-books","name":"Central Medical Library"},{"icon":"ti-flask","name":"Medical Laboratory Technology Labs"},{"icon":"ti-home","name":"Girls & Boys Hostels"},{"icon":"ti-bus","name":"Transport Facility"},{"icon":"ti-heartbeat","name":"Attached Government Hospital"},{"icon":"ti-shield","name":"Anti-Ragging Committee"},{"icon":"ti-heart","name":"Hospital Infection Control Committee"},{"icon":"ti-cpu","name":"Faculty Block with Modern Classrooms"},{"icon":"ti-medall","name":"Biomedical Waste Management"},{"icon":"ti-microphone","name":"Medical Education Unit"},{"icon":"ti-trophy","name":"Sports & Recreation"}],"placementRate":75,"avgPackage":"₹2.5 LPA","highestPackage":"₹5 LPA","placementYear":null,"admissionProcess":[{"title":"Meet Eligibility Criteria","desc":"Candidates must have completed 10+2 with Physics, Chemistry and Biology, with a minimum of 50% marks; minimum age 17 years."},{"title":"Apply via Tamil Nadu Allied Health Sciences Counselling","desc":"Register through the applicable Tamil Nadu government counselling process for Allied Health Sciences / paramedical seats."},{"title":"Choice Filling","desc":"Select Government Medical College Dindigul — B.Sc. MLT or the relevant certificate course as a preference during counselling."},{"title":"Document Verification & Seat Allotment","desc":"Complete document verification; seats allotted based on merit and category reservation, as seen in published merit/allotment lists."},{"title":"Reporting & Enrollment","desc":"Report to the college with original documents to confirm admission."}],"scholarships":["Tamil Nadu Government Scholarship Schemes (as applicable to Allied Health Sciences students)"],"events":["Dindigul Reads (Reading Initiative)","Marathon","Anti-Ragging Day/Week Celebration","CME Programs"],"distanceInfo":{"airport":"70 km (Madurai)","railway":"3 km (Dindigul Junction)","bustand":"4 km","metro":"N/A","hospital":"On Campus"},"hostelFeatures":["Separate Boys & Girls Hostels","Nasha Mukt (Drug-Free) Hostel Initiative"],"technicalClubs":["Medical Laboratory Technology Skill Club","Clinical Research Club"],"culturalClubs":["Dance Club","Music Club","Fine Arts Club"],"communityService":["Dindigul Reads Community Reading Programme","Marathon & Health Awareness Events","Anti-Ragging Awareness Campaigns"]}'),
('gandhigram-institute-of-rural-health-and-family-welfare-trust','gandhigram-institute-of-rural-health-and-family-welfare-trust','The Gandhigram Institute of Rural Health & Family Welfare Trust, Dindigul','GIRH&FWT Dindigul','allied-health-science','Autonomous Institute (Central Government, Ministry of Health & Family Welfare)','Government (Autonomous Body, Government of India)','1964','Gandhigram, Dindigul','Dindigul','Soundram Nagar, Gandhigram Post, Dindigul District - 624302, Tamil Nadu, India','https://maps.google.com/maps?q=The+Gandhigram+Institute+of+Rural+Health+Family+Welfare+Trust+Dindigul','https://girhfwt.org/courses/','+91 451 2999923','mailto:girhfwtdgl@rediffmail.com','https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Gandhigram-Institute-of-Rural-Health-and-Family-Welfare-Trust-Dindigul-collegeshine.webp','The Gandhigram Institute of Rural Health & Family - CollegeShine','The Gandhigram Institute of Rural Health & Family Welfare Trust, Dindigul is a government (autonomous body, government of india) allied health science.',NULL, '{"id":"gandhigram-institute-of-rural-health-and-family-welfare-trust","seo":{"metaTitle":"The Gandhigram Institute of Rural Health & Family - CollegeShine","metaDescription":"The Gandhigram Institute of Rural Health & Family Welfare Trust, Dindigul is a government (autonomous body, government of india) allied health science.","metaKeywords":["The Gandhigram Institute of Rural Health & Family Welfare Trust","Dindigul","GIRH&FWT Dindigul","The Gandhigram Institute of Rural Health & Family Welfare Trust","Dindigul admission 2026","The Gandhigram Institute of Rural Health & Family Welfare Trust","Dindigul fees","The Gandhigram Institute of Rural Health & Family Welfare Trust","Dindigul courses","Allied Health Science colleges in Dindigul","Gandhigram","Dindigul","Dindigul","Allied Health Science","Government (Autonomous Body","Government of India)","Autonomous Institute (Central Government","Ministry of Health & Family Welfare)","Autonomous Body under Ministry of Health & Family Welfare","Govt. of India","DMLT Recognized by Government of Tamil Nadu","PGDHPE Affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University","Curriculum for Health Visitors Course Approved by Indian Nursing Council (INC)","New Delhi","Diploma in Medical Laboratory Technology (DMLT)","PG Diploma in Health Promotion and Education (PGDHPE)","Health Visitors Course (Promotional Training for ANM/MPHW-F)"],"canonicalUrl":null,"robots":"index, follow","h1":"The Gandhigram Institute of Rural Health & Family Welfare Trust, Dindigul","openGraph":{"title":"The Gandhigram Institute of Rural Health & Family - CollegeShine","description":"The Gandhigram Institute of Rural Health & Family Welfare Trust, Dindigul is a government (autonomous body, government of india) allied health science.","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Gandhigram-Institute-of-Rural-Health-and-Family-Welfare-Trust-Dindigul-collegeshine.webp","type":"website","url":null},"twitterCard":{"card":"summary_large_image","title":"The Gandhigram Institute of Rural Health & Family - CollegeShine","description":"The Gandhigram Institute of Rural Health & Family Welfare Trust, Dindigul is a government (autonomous body, government of india) allied health science.","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Gandhigram-Institute-of-Rural-Health-and-Family-Welfare-Trust-Dindigul-collegeshine.webp"},"structuredData":{"schemaType":"CollegeOrUniversity","jsonLd":null,"includeFaqSchema":true,"includeBreadcrumbSchema":true}},"name":"The Gandhigram Institute of Rural Health & Family Welfare Trust, Dindigul","shortName":"GIRH&FWT Dindigul","tagline":"Promoting Rural Health & Family Welfare Since 1964","category":"allied-health-science","type":"Autonomous Institute (Central Government, Ministry of Health & Family Welfare)","ownership":"Government (Autonomous Body, Government of India)","established":1964,"location":"Gandhigram, Dindigul","district":"Dindigul","address":"Soundram Nagar, Gandhigram Post, Dindigul District - 624302, Tamil Nadu, India","mapLink":"https://maps.google.com/maps?q=The+Gandhigram+Institute+of+Rural+Health+Family+Welfare+Trust+Dindigul","mapQuery":"The+Gandhigram+Institute+of+Rural+Health+Family+Welfare+Trust+Dindigul","website":"https://girhfwt.org/courses/","phone":"+91 451 2999923","email":"mailto:girhfwtdgl@rediffmail.com","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Gandhigram-Institute-of-Rural-Health-and-Family-Welfare-Trust-Dindigul-collegeshine.webp","videoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/OPRJFVTD-KE?si=OqPyWx7n73Etefza&amp;start=13","affiliation":"Diploma in Medical Laboratory Technology (DMLT) recognized by Government of Tamil Nadu; PG Diploma in Health Promotion and Education (PGDHPE) affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University, Chennai; autonomous body under Ministry of Health & Family Welfare, Govt. of India","accreditation":["Autonomous Body under Ministry of Health & Family Welfare, Govt. of India","DMLT Recognized by Government of Tamil Nadu","PGDHPE Affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University","Curriculum for Health Visitors Course Approved by Indian Nursing Council (INC), New Delhi","Houses a Population Research Centre (PRC) — One of 18 PRCs in India"],"about":"The Gandhigram Institute of Rural Health & Family Welfare Trust (GIRH&FWT) was established in 1964 by Dr. T.S. Soundram, with support from the Government of Tamil Nadu, the Government of India, and the Ford Foundation. It functions today as an autonomous body under the Ministry of Health & Family Welfare, Government of India, with the objective of promoting the implementation of National Health and Family Welfare programmes in rural areas through training, research, and community outreach.\\n\\nThe institute offers three pioneer training courses: the Diploma in Medical Laboratory Technology (DMLT), a 2-year, 30-seat programme recognized by the Government of Tamil Nadu; the Post Graduate Diploma in Health Promotion and Education (PGDHPE), a 12-month, 30-seat programme affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University, Chennai; and the Health Visitors Course, a 6-month promotional training programme for registered ANM/MPHW(F) health workers, with curriculum approved by the Indian Nursing Council (INC), New Delhi. The institute also houses a Population Research Centre (PRC) — one of 18 PRCs operating in India — which has been conducting research in maternal and child health, fertility, mortality, family planning, and rural health since 1959, alongside its Health & Family Welfare Training Centre (HFWTC), Department of Health Promotion and Education (DHPE), and Rural Health Training and Technology Institute (RHTTI) units.","highlights":["Established 1964 — Autonomous Body, Govt. of India","DMLT — 2-Year Diploma, 30 Seats, Govt. of Tamil Nadu Recognized","PGDHPE — Affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University","Health Visitors Course — INC-Approved Curriculum for ANM/MPHW(F)","Houses Population Research Centre (PRC) — One of 18 in India","Multiple Specialized Units: HFWTC, DHPE, RHTTI, Central Unit","60+ Years of Rural Health & Family Welfare Training","Strong Community Interface — Health Camps & Outreach Programmes"],"departments":[{"name":"Diploma in Medical Laboratory Technology (DMLT)","level":"Diploma"},{"name":"PG Diploma in Health Promotion and Education (PGDHPE)","level":"PG"},{"name":"Health Visitors Course (Promotional Training for ANM/MPHW-F)","level":"UG"}],"facilities":[{"icon":"ti-wifi","name":"Institute Network"},{"icon":"ti-books","name":"Institute Library"},{"icon":"ti-flask","name":"Medical Laboratory Technology Labs"},{"icon":"ti-home","name":"Hostel Facility"},{"icon":"ti-bus","name":"Transport Facility"},{"icon":"ti-heartbeat","name":"Health & Family Welfare Training Centre (HFWTC)"},{"icon":"ti-crown","name":"Population Research Centre (PRC)"},{"icon":"ti-heart","name":"Rural Health Training & Technology Institute (RHTTI)"},{"icon":"ti-trophy","name":"Sports & Recreation"},{"icon":"ti-microphone","name":"Department of Health Promotion & Education (DHPE)"},{"icon":"ti-cpu","name":"Central Unit"},{"icon":"ti-medall","name":"Kshamta Kendra (Special Programme)"}],"placementRate":70,"avgPackage":"₹2 LPA","highestPackage":"₹4 LPA","placementYear":null,"admissionProcess":[{"title":"Meet Eligibility Criteria","desc":"For DMLT: pass in HSC with Physics, Chemistry, Botany/Zoology or Biology (age 17-32, 37 for SC/ST). For PGDHPE: a Master''s degree with 1 year community-work experience, or a Bachelor''s degree with 2 years community/public-health experience."},{"title":"Download Prospectus & Application","desc":"Download the relevant course prospectus and application form from the official website."},{"title":"Submit Application","desc":"Complete and submit the application form along with required documents before the deadline."},{"title":"Merit-Based Selection","desc":"Seats are allotted based on merit and eligibility as per institute norms (30 seats each for DMLT and PGDHPE)."},{"title":"Reporting & Enrollment","desc":"Report to the institute with original documents to confirm admission."}],"scholarships":[],"events":["Health Camps","Community Outreach Programmes","Sports Meet","Cultural Events","Training Programmes (Statistical/Technical)"],"distanceInfo":{"airport":"75 km (Madurai)","railway":"12 km (Dindigul Junction)","bustand":"10 km","metro":"N/A","hospital":"On Campus (HFWTC)"},"hostelFeatures":["Hostel Facility Available","Mess Facility"],"technicalClubs":["Medical Laboratory Technology Skill Club","Public Health Research Club"],"culturalClubs":["Cultural Events Committee"],"communityService":["Health Camps in Rural Areas","Reproductive & Child Health Research (via PRC)","Family Planning Awareness Programmes","Community Outreach & Public Health Education"]}'),
