on and Control","Parent Institution is an IDF (International Diabetes Federation) Centre of Education","Joint Programme with Deakin University","Australia (Diabetes Nurse Educators Course)","B.Sc. Medical Laboratory Technology (MLT)","Certificate — Physician Assistantship","Certificate — Ophthalmic Nursing Assistant","Certificate — Diabetes Technologies","National Diabetes Education Program (NDEP)"],"canonicalUrl":null,"robots":"index, follow","h1":"Dr. Mohan''s Diabetes Education Academy (DMDEA), Chennai","openGraph":{"title":"Dr. Mohan''s Diabetes Education Academy (DMDEA) - CollegeShine","description":"Dr. Mohan''s Diabetes Education Academy (DMDEA), Chennai is a private (dr. mohan''s diabetes specialities centre group) allied health science college in.","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Dr.-Mohans-Diabetes-Specialities-Centre-Chennai-collegeshine.webp","type":"website","url":null},"twitterCard":{"card":"summary_large_image","title":"Dr. Mohan''s Diabetes Education Academy (DMDEA) - CollegeShine","description":"Dr. Mohan''s Diabetes Education Academy (DMDEA), Chennai is a private (dr. mohan''s diabetes specialities centre group) allied health science college in.","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Dr.-Mohans-Diabetes-Specialities-Centre-Chennai-collegeshine.webp"},"structuredData":{"schemaType":"CollegeOrUniversity","jsonLd":null,"includeFaqSchema":true,"includeBreadcrumbSchema":true}},"name":"Dr. Mohan''s Diabetes Education Academy (DMDEA), Chennai","shortName":"Dr. Mohan''s Diabetes Education Academy","tagline":"Towards Excellence in Diabetes Care Training","category":"allied-health-science","type":"Private Specialized Medical Education Academy","ownership":"Private (Dr. Mohan''s Diabetes Specialities Centre Group)","established":2008,"location":"Gopalapuram, Chennai","district":"Chennai","address":"No.6-B, Conran Smith Road, Near Satyam Cinemas, Gopalapuram, Chennai, Tamil Nadu 600086","mapLink":"https://maps.google.com/?q=Dr+Mohans+Diabetes+Specialities+Centre+Gopalapuram+Chennai","mapQuery":"Dr+Mohans+Diabetes+Specialities+Centre+Gopalapuram+Chennai","website":"https://diabetescourses.in/non_physicican.html","phone":"+91 96771 88888","email":"mailto:info@drmohans.com","image":"https://collegeshine.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Dr.-Mohans-Diabetes-Specialities-Centre-Chennai-collegeshine.webp","videoUrl":"https://www.youtube.com/embed/BvoA6eLHVU8?si=XTpiA0RwfWwRswNK","affiliation":"B.Sc. Medical Laboratory Technology affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University; Deakin-DMDEA Diabetes Nurse Educators course jointly offered with Deakin University, Australia; parent institution (DMDSC) is a WHO Collaborating Centre for Noncommunicable Diseases and an IDF Centre of Education","accreditation":["Affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University (for B.Sc. MLT & Select Courses)","Parent Institution (DMDSC) is a WHO Collaborating Centre for Noncommunicable Diseases Prevention and Control","Parent Institution is an IDF (International Diabetes Federation) Centre of Education","Joint Programme with Deakin University, Australia (Diabetes Nurse Educators Course)"],"about":"Dr. Mohan''s Diabetes Education Academy (DMDEA) was established in September 2008 under the leadership of Prof. V. Mohan, internationally acclaimed diabetologist and research scientist, and the late Dr. (Mrs.) M. Rema, a well-known specialist in diabetic eye disease. The Academy offers specialized training in diabetes and its complications to doctors, nurses, lab technicians, and other paramedical personnel through varied and innovative courses, many offered for the first time in India.\\n\\nDMDEA benefits from its association with its parent institution, Dr. Mohan''s Diabetes Specialities Centre (DMDSC), a WHO Collaborating Centre for Noncommunicable Diseases Prevention and Control and an IDF (International Diabetes Federation) Centre of Education. Its activities have been acknowledged by The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University, which has granted affiliation to the Academy for several of its courses. On the allied health science side, DMDEA offers a B.Sc. in Medical Laboratory Technology (3-year degree plus 1-year internship), alongside one-year certificate courses in Physician Assistantship, Ophthalmic Nursing Assistant, and Diabetes Technologies, a 10-month National Diabetes Education Program (NDEP) for diploma/B.Sc./M.Sc. holders in nutrition, nursing, or life sciences, and the Deakin-DMDEA Course for Diabetes Nurse Educators — a 4-month international programme jointly offered with Deakin University, Australia, for practicing nurses.","highlights":["Established 2008 Under Prof. V. Mohan & Late Dr. M. Rema","B.Sc. Medical Laboratory Technology — Affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. M.G.R. Medical University","4 One-Year Certificate Courses — Physician Assistantship, Ophthalmic Nursing Assistant, Diabetes Technologies & More","National Diabetes Education Program (NDEP) — 10-Month Diabetes Educator Training","Deakin-DMDEA Course for Diabetes Nurse Educators — International Programme with Deakin University, Australia","Parent Institution is a WHO Collaborating Centre & IDF Centre of Education","Training at India''s Leading Diabetes Care Network (Est. 1991, 34 Cities, 51 Centres)","Courses Offered for the First Time in India in the Field of Diabetology"],"departments":[{"name":"B.Sc. Medical Laboratory Technology (MLT)","level":"UG"},{"name":"Certificate — Physician Assistantship","level":"UG"},{"name":"Certificate — Ophthalmic Nursing Assistant","level":"UG"},{"name":"Certificate — Diabetes Technologies","level":"UG"},{"name":"National Diabetes Education Program (NDEP)","level":"UG"},{"name":"Deakin-DMDEA Course for Diabetes Nurse Educators","level":"UG"}],"facilities":[{"icon":"ti-wifi","name":"Academy Network"},{"icon":"ti-books","name":"Diabetology Resource Library"},{"icon":"ti-flask","name":"Diabetes Laboratory & Biomedical Equipment Training"},{"icon":"ti-heartbeat","name":"Attached Diabetes Specialities Hospital (DMDSC)"},{"icon":"ti-crown","name":"IP Facility Access for Clinical Training"},{"icon":"ti-heart","name":"Eye Care Department (for Ophthalmic Assistant Training)"},{"icon":"ti-cpu","name":"Modules-Based Digital Learning (NDEP & Deakin Courses)"},{"icon":"ti-medall","name":"Research Association with Madras Diabetes Research Foundation"},{"icon":"ti-microphone","name":"Contact Classes & Weekend Training Sessions"},{"icon":"ti-trophy","name":"International Collaboration — Deakin University, Australia"}],"placementRate":80,"avgPackage":"₹2.5 LPA","highestPackage":"₹5 LPA","placementYear":null,"admissionProcess":[{"title":"Meet Course-Specific Eligibility","desc":"Eligibility varies by course: B.Sc. MLT requires a pass in +2 with a University eligibility certificate; certificate courses require +2/HSC pass (age limit up to 25); NDEP requires a Diploma/B.Sc./M.Sc. in relevant fields (age 21+); Deakin course requires a B.Sc./GNM in Nursing."},{"title":"Review the Admissions Procedure","desc":"Refer to the official Admissions Procedure page on diabetescourses.in for the current application cycle and requirements."},{"title":"Submit Application","desc":"Complete and submit the application form for the desired course along with required academic documents."},{"title":"Interview / Document Verification","desc":"Shortlisted candidates undergo document verification and, for select courses, an interview or interaction with faculty."},{"title":"Enrollment & Orientation","desc":"Confirmed candidates report for orientation and begin the programme, which for full-time certificate courses runs on a non-residential basis."}],"scholarships":[],"events":["Diabetes Update (Annual CME Conference)","Contact Classes & Weekend Training Sessions (Deakin Course)","World Diabetes Day Awareness Programs"],"distanceInfo":{"airport":"18 km (Chennai International Airport)","railway":"5 km (Chennai Central)","bustand":"4 km","metro":"2 km (Nearest Metro Station)","hospital":"On Campus (DMDSC Head Office)"},"hostelFeatures":[],"technicalClubs":["Diabetes Technology & Biomedical Equipment Club","Clinical Research Association"],"culturalClubs":[],"communityService":["World Diabetes Day Awareness Programs","Community Diabetes Screening Camps","Public Health Education on Noncommunicable Diseases (via WHO Collaborating Centre mandate)"]}'),
