sults?search_query=Tamil+Nadu+Government+Music+College+Coimbatore","affiliation":"The Tamil Nadu Dr. J. Jayalalithaa Music and Fine Arts University, Chennai","accreditation":["Government of Tamil Nadu Institution","Department of Art and Culture, Government of Tamil Nadu","Affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. J. Jayalalithaa Music and Fine Arts University"],"about":"Tamil Nadu Government Music College, Coimbatore was established in 1993 under the Department of Art and Culture, Government of Tamil Nadu, with the objective of promoting and preserving fine arts and traditional music. The institution initially functioned from the Corporation Building at R.S. Puram and offered training in Vocal, Veena, Violin and Musicology. Dance was introduced in 1994 and Music Teacher Training was introduced in 1999. The college subsequently moved to its own building at Malumichampatti, about 15 kilometres from Coimbatore city.\\n\\nFrom the academic year 2014-2015, the institution has offered B.A. Music programmes in Vocal, Veena and Violin, while an Evening Music College was introduced in 2016-2017 for Vocal, Veena and Violin. The institution conducts programmes in traditional music and dance, with examinations and certificates administered through the Tamil Nadu Dr. J. Jayalalithaa Music and Fine Arts University. The college functions as a government institution dedicated to developing students in Indian classical music and performing arts.","highlights":["Established in 1993","Government Institution under Tamil Nadu Department of Art and Culture","Located at Malumichampatti, Coimbatore","Affiliated to Tamil Nadu Dr. J. Jayalalithaa Music and Fine Arts University","Three-Year B.A. Music Degree Programmes","Three-Year Diploma Programmes in Music and Dance","One-Year Music Teacher Training Programme","Two-Year Evening Certificate Courses","Training in Vocal, Veena and Violin","Training in Thavil and Nadaswaram","Bharathanatyam Training","Government Scholarship and Free Bus Pass Benefits"]