d Fine Arts University","Recognized Research Centre for Ph.D. in Music","Recognized Performing Arts Institution"],"about":"Sri Sathguru Sangeetha Vidyalayam is a historic institution dedicated to Indian Carnatic music and performing arts in Madurai. The Vidyalayam commenced evening classes in Vocal and Instrumental Music in 1959 and subsequently developed into a College of Music. It was affiliated to Madurai Kamaraj University in 1966. The institution is housed in Lakshmi Sundaram Hall and has been associated with the promotion, teaching and preservation of Indian classical performing arts for several decades.\\n\\nThe college offers undergraduate and postgraduate programmes in Music, with Vocal and Veena as major disciplines and Vocal, Veena, Violin, Mridangam and Bharathanatyam as allied areas. The institution was recognized as a research centre for Ph.D. in Music in 2012. Seminars, workshops, symposiums, live concerts, monthly music programmes, annual concert series and Composer''s Day celebrations form an important part of its academic and cultural activities. The institution is managed by a committee and is listed by the Tamil Nadu Government as a government-aided affiliated institution.","highlights":["Established in 1959","Historic College of Music in Madurai","Government Aided Institution","Affiliated with Tamil Nadu Music and Fine Arts University","College affiliated to Madurai Kamaraj University since 1966","B.A. Music Degree Programme","M.A. Music Degree Programme","Ph.D. Research Centre in Music","Vocal and Veena Major Disciplines","Violin, Mridangam and Bharathanatyam Allied Disciplines","Regular Seminars, Workshops and Symposiums","Monthly Music Concerts and Cultural Programmes"],"departments":[{"name":"B.A. Music - Vocal","level":"UG"},{"name":"B.A. Music - Veena","level":"UG"},{"name":"M.A. Music - Vocal","level":"PG"},{"name":"M.A. Music - Veena","level":"PG"},{"name":"Ph.D. in Music","level":"PhD"},{"name":"Certificate / Value Added Courses","level