ivate self-financing institution in Coimbatore associated with Lalit Kalakshetra and affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. J. Jayalalithaa Music and Fine Arts University. The institution traces its establishment to 1992 and operates its college campus at Kalagram, Raj Bhavan, 4/1 Attukkal Road, Thondamuthur, Coimbatore - 641109, while its administrative/admissions presence is listed at R.S. Puram, Coimbatore. The Tamil Nadu Department of Art and Culture and the Tamil Nadu Dr. J. Jayalalithaa Music and Fine Arts University list Raviraj College of Fine Arts among the self-financing fine arts colleges in Tamil Nadu.\\n\\nThe college provides undergraduate and postgraduate education in fine arts and performing arts. Its official 2025-26 admission application lists B.F.A. in Painting as a four-year regular programme, B.A. in Bharathanatyam as a three-year regular programme and M.F.A. in Painting as a three-year weekend programme. The institution''s official website additionally identifies B.A. Music and M.A. Bharathanatyam among the Raviraj College programmes. The college and its parent institution emphasize painting, dance, music, cultural education, exhibitions, workshops and practical artistic training.","highlights":["Established in 1992","Self-Financing Fine Arts College","Affiliated to The Tamil Nadu Dr. J. Jayalalithaa Music and Fine Arts University","B.F.A. Painting Programme","B.A. Bharathanatyam Programme","M.F.A. Painting Programme","B.A. Music Programme","M.A. Bharathanatyam Programme","Kalagram College Campus at Thondamuthur","Professional Fine Arts and Performing Arts Training","Art Exhibitions and Cultural Activities","Strong Association with Lalit Kalakshetra"],"departments":[{"name":"B.F.A. Painting","level":"UG"},{"name":"B.A. Bharathanatyam","level":"UG"},{"name":"B.A. Music","level":"UG"},{"name":"M.F.A. Painting","level":"PG"},{"name":"M.A. Bharathanatyam","level":"PG"}],"facilities":[{"icon":"ti-palette","name":"Painting Studios"},{"icon":"ti-music","name":"Music Training Facilities"},{"icon":"ti-microphone","name":"Dance & Performing Arts Facilities"},{"icon":"ti-image","name":"Art Exhibition Facilities"},{"icon":"ti-camera","name":"Photography / Visual Documentation Facilities"},{"icon":"ti-book","name":"Art & Cultural Learning Resources"},{"icon":"ti-home","name":"Kalagram Campus"},{"icon":"ti-blackboard","name":"Classroom Facilities"},{"icon":"ti-users","name":"Workshop & Training Facilities"},{"icon":"ti-calendar","name":"Cultural Event Facilities"},{"icon":"ti-trophy","name":"Exhibition & Competition Support"},{"icon":"ti-world","name":"Art & Cultural Outreach"}],"placementRate":"Approx. 70%","avgPackage":"Approx. ₹3.0 LPA","highestPackage":"Approx. ₹6.0 LPA","placementYear":null,"admissionProcess":[{"title":"Select the Appropriate Programme","desc":"Applicants can choose from the fine arts and performing arts programmes offered by the college."},{"title":"Obtain the College Application","desc":"The college publishes programme-specific admission application forms through its official website."},{"title":"Submit Academic Documents","desc":"Applicants are required to provide the academic and personal details requested in the admission application."},{"title":"Programme Eligibility Verification","desc":"The college verifies eligibility according to the applicable university and programme requirements."},{"title":"Admission Confirmation","desc":"Eligible applicants complete the admission and fee-payment process according to the college''s instructions."}],"scholarships":["Ranilakshmi Memorial Scholarship","Approx. Merit-based Financial Assistance","Approx. Need-based Financial Assistance","Approx. Government Scholarship Schemes","Approx. Category-based Scholarship Schemes"],"events":["National Exhibition of Art","Kalagram Village Folk Art Fair","South Indian Artists'' Camp","Art Exhibitions","Painting Workshops","Bharathanatyam Programmes","Music and Cultural Events","Fine Arts Training Workshops"],"distanceInfo"