yv4EYp0","affiliation":"Affiliated to Tamil Nadu Music and Fine Arts University","accreditation":["Affiliated to Tamil Nadu Music and Fine Arts University","Affiliated / recognized through the Tamil Nadu Music and Fine Arts University academic system","Listed by Tamil Nadu Department of Art and Culture","Self-Financing Institution under Tamil Isai Sangam"],"about":"Tamil Isai Kalloori functions under Tamil Isai Sangam at Raja Annamalai Mandram, Chennai. Tamil Isai Sangam was founded in 1943 with the objective of promoting and preserving Tamil Isai. The college is documented as having been established in 1995 and provides structured education and training in Tamil music and related performing arts. The institution is located at No.5, Esplanade Road, Chennai - 600108. Official Tamil Isai Sangam admission material identifies the college as affiliated to the Tamil Nadu Music and Fine Arts University.\\\\n\\\\nThe institution offers undergraduate, postgraduate, diploma, teacher-training and certificate-level programmes in music and performing arts. Its academic and practical areas include Vocal, Veena, Violin, Flute, Mridangam, Tavil, Nagaswaram, Thirumurai Isai, Bharatanatyam and Nattuvangam. The institution also conducts the Tamil Isai Sangam Grade Examination through its TISGEC programme, with eight grades and examinations conducted at six-month intervals. The institution maintains music-related research resources including a library containing rare books, musical instruments and an auditorium.","highlights":["Established in 1995","Functions under Tamil Isai Sangam","Located at Raja Annamalai Mandram, Chennai","Affiliated to Tamil Nadu Music and Fine Arts University","Dedicated institution for Tamil music and performing arts","Undergraduate and postgraduate music programmes","Diploma and certificate programmes","Training in Vocal, Veena, Violin and other instruments","Bharatanatyam and Nattuvangam training","Thirumurai Isai training","Tamil Isai Sangam Grade Examinati